#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193040 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80f239b0-bc36-5735-804d-d1f9e0c37937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191090} {:answer/id #uuid "c026a4f0-44ed-5b53-95aa-472e28befe35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191091} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ca2fe4-5e43-5af9-8684-2d550bff4311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191092} {:answer/id #uuid "329fe08b-9018-556f-ac99-f175fbbad450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191093} {:answer/id #uuid "49f2e517-e7df-5358-ad0a-0deb8e21d36e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9ca2fe4-5e43-5af9-8684-2d550bff4311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191092} :answer-field/id #uuid "e253ec61-3e97-5ee7-b646-84625a2dba57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1eb8e242-f7cb-5632-a09c-62dcc98103d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161445" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc6718f6-4976-57b6-b370-f79e3466cb78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332160} {:answer/id #uuid "3eda1123-fb27-58ee-b348-baf8461c20c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332161} {:answer/id #uuid "0c1363c9-8a00-510f-a8af-9a584d6f4f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332162} {:answer/id #uuid "f3aed6ca-2b03-5dde-a451-aa62b960f5b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332163} {:answer/id #uuid "9be9472c-4118-5314-9f01-1e88064b98a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9be9472c-4118-5314-9f01-1e88064b98a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332164} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ad2ca6b-d482-5608-9f02-2e57e713f54b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "318629c1-2457-50a8-91b8-67b30dc4061b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161624" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8414de2e05da43c03fae3c8b1ff2102401e990188e9fd4ee59a24308ec34b086.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we have seen, $∂A$ consists of two concentric circles: the outer one is in $A,$ while the inner one is not.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ contains some of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07cb221d-6254-54c9-b93b-66f9c21ca222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y\\le x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332167} {:answer/id #uuid "6f724aae-8b8f-5b82-bac0-67f022cb60ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\le y\\le x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332168} {:answer/id #uuid "1befd6ec-4f43-5a5a-90de-6227f6e4bdee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\le y<x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332169} {:answer/id #uuid "fd49e677-9cf8-59d2-abc2-ae8a5ae11b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x<y<x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332170} {:answer/id #uuid "1f006973-3acf-581b-842a-d7f56833fef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y<x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd49e677-9cf8-59d2-abc2-ae8a5ae11b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x<y<x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332170} :answer-field/id #uuid "85c065e2-d4a7-5f6e-aa29-d60489c19beb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cae3814-ea99-54e9-86e7-c0bc019bdf37" :question/math-academy-id "q-161718" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/af1e6e7b384732a527fc77e9729c6e02aaa288d4076c030c9fae58742cb10f74.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/0a0b92621d83d6395926a75b5cae34f479a8b9e64dfe82711094c3724b3b3220.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/3ddef68bf4b4284c1b68896920fddb8d7fb0e70eba15dee103cdbc0134a9ed20.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-x<y<x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da8d515-7cc0-506d-abb2-6c7a21926771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332174} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2617a0-7b87-51fe-9e98-a57527022afa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332175} {:answer/id #uuid "2f2db1fd-ef9f-52cf-8fd2-c24e6c710a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332176} {:answer/id #uuid "8761eec8-3cc6-5877-b192-11245ef0e21c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332177} {:answer/id #uuid "fb486883-b547-52d1-b198-5104c36a9bbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0da8d515-7cc0-506d-abb2-6c7a21926771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332174} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9210ab2-eeb9-5f7b-b9eb-272b79a0921a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02d084df-878c-5b52-8acb-7b7ee4dbdd09" :question/math-academy-id "q-161730" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/aa335a55f5b4496cdaccca5d35e286a168598761188bc520c81397ef136f927d.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/fba9ba3e52ed19eb0bb2286ae59c49bb9dc648134d9eab3c4e2d13862963f736.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/2f3cd30dbaa4f84c43f2a7f1197aa904e3d43b1212241ae26736b2a0087f6170.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200e92b1-e2b3-5589-979a-cfdf33ec04bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332181} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e4940b-f327-53ce-8c5d-416061ae5ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}x<y<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332182} {:answer/id #uuid "ff23d5f1-240e-57b7-b037-2856b86c8238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le y\\le \\frac{2}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332183} {:answer/id #uuid "9db3281b-b340-5f08-8e81-e177d5ceb825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332184} {:answer/id #uuid "12f3fa0f-8c5d-50ca-a4ae-20b159472d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "200e92b1-e2b3-5589-979a-cfdf33ec04bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332181} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed9b2810-dcbe-5c0f-b69b-0d58bc3542a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7db58d1f-c945-5982-b978-7bc405280419" :question/math-academy-id "q-161731" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8d7ceac8c936a745ae79f71844a6d1a74175b1b97a2a497588d34c9ff988cdf9.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/c0e6ef400b15c54264a400af99bef64c3bb5aeb7ceadbdd599375c0f1e0d3642.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8c5bbdfca6736194791f834ab4aadb03a30e3f116e89ffd5a7ea3e0104708ae4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x}.\n$$"}]}
